WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  That the Maven the mandated build command will use was ALREADY PRESENT on this
  host at exactly the version the pinned pom requires, so that ./build/mvn's
  install_mvn() download branch cannot be taken. A download is an installation,
  and this run is forbidden to install, upgrade or substitute any tool
  (AAP 0.4.3, 0.8.1, 0.8.3). The check therefore PREVENTS rather than DISCOVERS:
  it runs BEFORE the build command, and no command in this file invokes
  ./build/mvn.

  This is the ONE version check in the whole run that halts rather than records
  and continues. AAP 0.9.3 carves Maven out of the record-and-continue rule
  explicitly: drift is record-and-continue only where recording it is all that is
  needed, and here continuing would require the prohibited install. AAP 0.9.2
  states the halting condition as 'the resolvable Maven not being exactly 3.9.11,
  such that the wrapper would download one'.

